course: dictionary
lesson: 13126
title: One word, many meanings
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: One word can have more than one meaning. You can often find the right one by reading the words around it, which are its context. «We put a flyer through every letterbox on the street.» Letterboxes and putting something through them tell you a flyer must be something you can post, so here it means a small printed sheet.
explain: The same word can mean something very different in another sentence. «The eagle is a strong flyer, soaring high above the hills.» Soaring and hills tell you a flyer is a bird, or anything that flies. Always ask: what would fit here? Then try your meaning in the sentence and check that it makes sense.
explain: Sport gives the word a quick, informal meaning. «Sam got off to a flyer and was ahead after ten seconds.» Ten seconds is a short time, so a flyer here is a very fast start. If you are not sure, read on for more clues, or check a dictionary.
fact: A flyer is a small printed sheet of paper that advertises an event, shop or service.
fact: A flyer can also be a person or thing that flies, such as a pilot, a passenger who flies often, or a bird.
fact: In sport, informally, a flyer is a very fast start or a very fast runner or player.
fact: «Frequent flyer» means a passenger who travels on planes a lot.
fact: Flier is another spelling of flyer, and both can be used for the same meanings.
exercise: «We put a flyer through every letterbox on the street.» What is a flyer here? | A bird that lives on the street | A runner in a race | *A small printed sheet advertising an event | A pilot who flies planes
exercise: «Sam got off to a flyer and was ahead after ten seconds.» What does flyer mean here? | A paper advertisement | A kite made of paper | A passenger on a plane | *A very fast start, in sport
exercise: «The eagle is a strong flyer, soaring high above the hills.» What is a flyer in this sentence? | A printed sheet of paper | *A bird, or anything that flies | A very slow runner | A shop that sells kites
test: «Dad is a frequent flyer, so he has been on many planes.» Here, a flyer means? | *A passenger who flies often | A kite | A very fast start in a race | A printed advert
test: Which spelling is another correct spelling of flyer? | Floyer | Flyar | Flyr | *Flier
exam: «The flyers on the school gate said the fair starts at noon, so Maya got there early.» What does flyers mean here? | Pilots who fly to the fair | Fast runners on the path | *Printed sheets advertising the fair | Birds that fly over the gate
